    "annotations": {
      "summary": "A model invented a value, a date, a citation or a drug name, and the answer was withheld.",
      "description": "Nothing reached a physician: the summary was refused, the screen degraded per D-15, and the finding is a row in core.ai_grounding_defect. The alert is warning rather than critical for exactly that reason — the safety property held. It fires anyway because §10.6's fifth permanent invariant is about a class of failure whose *rate* is the thing worth knowing, and because CP72 records these as defects precisely so that somebody looks at them rather than a retry making them disappear. Five minutes rather than instantly, so that one odd answer during a deploy does not page anybody.",
      "runbook": "Open /v1/ops/ai/grounding-defects and read the newest. The excerpt shows the sentence and the arm shows what kind of failure it was: CITATION is usually the prompt, NUMBER and DATE are usually the model, DRUG is expected until CP75 supplies a formulary. Classify it — TRUE_POSITIVE, FALSE_POSITIVE or VALIDATOR_DEFECT — because that classification is the only source of the false-positive rate any future argument about loosening the check will be made with."
    }
  },
