    "annotations": {
      "summary": "Answers are being passed as grounded by a check that looked at no tokens at all.",
      "description": "**This is the failure the whole mechanism is most likely to have, and it is invisible on every other panel.** A clean grounding rate from a check that examined nothing looks exactly like a healthy system: the verdicts say PASSED, the defect count is zero, and summaries reach physicians unchecked. It happens when the payload's fact index stops decoding, when an agent's prose field is renamed, or when a payload arrives empty. Critical rather than warning because the safety property is *not* holding while this is true, unlike every other alert on this page.",
      "runbook": "Open the AI quality dashboard's 'Tokens the check examined' panel and confirm the series is flat. Then open one recent interaction at /v1/ops/ai/interactions and look at outbound.payload: if it has no `facts` array, the assembler is at fault; if it has one, the answer's prose fields are not where the check is looking. Until it is fixed, treat every AI summary as unverified."
    }
